#. Tag: title
#: guides.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid "Detailed Guides"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:45
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This chapter describes how to perform some common tasks in &kpresenter;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: guides.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid "Create a <acronym>HTML</acronym> Slideshow"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:51
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Turn an existing presentation into standard <acronym>HTML</acronym> pages "
"with accompanying navigation aids."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First, either make a new presentation, or open an existing one. Then, click "
"on <guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Create HTML Slideshow...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: guides.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>File menu option to <guimenuitem>Create HTML Slideshow...</"
"guimenuitem></screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: guides.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase>File menu option to <guimenuitem>Create HTML Slideshow...</"
"guimenuitem></phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "A dialog box asks if you want to use a previously saved configuration:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: guides.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Previous configuration dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: guides.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Previous configuration dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click <guibutton>No</guibutton> if this is the first time that you have used "
"this feature, or if you want to alter specific options. The <guibutton>Yes</"
"guibutton> option allows you to use details that you have previously entered "
"for your <acronym>HTML</acronym> slideshow, so that you can quickly create "
"the slideshow without needing to adjust the options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid "You will then get a dialog box asking for a few details:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: guides.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>Fill in the details for your <acronym>HTML</acronym> slideshow</"
"screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: guides.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase>Fill in the details for your <acronym>HTML</acronym> slideshow</"
"phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Fill in each field (the dialog takes the informations from &kcontrolcenter; "
"if they exist) and ensure that the path details are correct, as this is "
"where &kpresenter; will save your new <acronym>HTML</acronym> files and "
"pictures. Click on the <guibutton>Next</guibutton> when you are done."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the path you select at this stage does not exist, &kpresenter; will ask "
"if you would like to create it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid "Now you can configure the specific <acronym>HTML</acronym> options:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: guides.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>Fill in additional details for your <acronym>HTML</acronym> "
"slideshow</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: guides.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase>Fill in additional details for your <acronym>HTML</acronym> "
"slideshow</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here, the encoding and format details can be changed, along with the zoom "
"level of the slides. For example, if you originally designed your slides to "
"display full screen on a 1280 x 1024 resolution screen, you could scale the "
"slides to 50% to enable them to be easily viewed in a much smaller web "
"browser window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In most cases, the defaults will be fine, and you can safely press the "
"<guibutton>Next</guibutton> to continue to the next page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid "Now you can customize the colors of the web pages:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: guides.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>Setting up the display style for your <acronym>HTML</acronym> "
"slideshow</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: guides.docbook:152
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase>Setting up the display style for your <acronym>HTML</acronym> "
"slideshow</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:158
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When &kpresenter; creates the web pages for you, the text colors for the "
"navigation aids will follow whatever you set here. To change any of these "
"colors, click the colored bar next to the corresponding text label. The "
"colors used in your actual slides will be unchanged."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:163
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose colors that are complementary to the contents of your presentation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:167
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guibutton>Next</guibutton> button presents a dialog box that allows you "
"to change the name used on the <acronym>HTML</acronym> page for each slide:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: guides.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Setting the slide names</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: guides.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Setting the slide names</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If your presentation was intended to be displayed in an unattended manner "
"(&ie; automatic advance to next slide, &etc;), you can also make your "
"<acronym>HTML</acronym> presentation counterpart exhibit the same behavior:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: guides.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Unattended presentations</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: guides.docbook:196
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Unattended presentations</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here, you can force the slide to advance to the next after a specified "
"amount of time, and also make the presentation return to the start once it "
"reaches the end."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now it is time to actually produce your <acronym>HTML</acronym> "
"presentation, the progress of which is shown in this dialog box:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: guides.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Saving your configuration</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: guides.docbook:217
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Saving your configuration</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:221
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Finally, you can save the configuration you have just used before you close "
"the dialog box by pressing the <guibutton>Save Configuration...</guibutton> "
"button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:227
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"What we now have are the newly-produced <filename>html/</filename> and "
"<filename>pics/</filename> folders, created where we earlier set the path:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: guides.docbook:232
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>The newly created <acronym>HTML</acronym> slideshow folders</"
"screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: guides.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase>The newly created <acronym>HTML</acronym> slideshow folders</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is also an <filename>index.html</filename> file to launch your web "
"slideshow."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:248
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can see how it works by using your file manager or web browser to open "
"the <filename>index.html</filename> file. Click where prompted, and the "
"first slide of your presentation is displayed. It will now behave as a "
"&kpresenter; slideshow."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each click on the arrow icons take you to the next or previous slide. To get "
"back to the start of the slideshow click on the slide icon."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:256
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To share your presentation with the world, transfer the newly-produced files "
"to a network-accessible location (&ie; webspace), remembering to keep the "
"folder structure intact."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: guides.docbook:262
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Exporting &kpresenter; presentations to a <trademark>Memory Stick</trademark>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:264
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Some Sony projectors have the ability to run a presentation directly from a "
"<trademark>Memory Stick</trademark>, without needing to connect a computer "
"up to the projector. &kpresenter; can export presentations to the format "
"required by these projectors, and this tutorial will show you how to export "
"your presentation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:272
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each exported slideshow consists of a series of image files (one for each "
"slide in the original presentation, plus two title slides) and an index "
"file. They are created in a fairly complex folder structure that allows more "
"than one presentation to be stored on a single memory stick. A simple "
"example is shown below, consisting of two presentations."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: guides.docbook:285
#, no-c-format
msgid "<trademark>Memory Stick</trademark> folder structure"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:293
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the presentation that you want to export is not already open, go to "
"<guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Open...</guimenuitem> and select the "
"presentation that you want to export."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:301
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now, select the <guimenu>File</guimenu> menu and choose <guimenuitem>Create "
"Memory Stick Slideshow...</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: guides.docbook:307
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>The &kpresenter; <guimenuitem>Create Memory Stick Slideshow...</"
"guimenuitem> menu selection.</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: guides.docbook:313
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase>The &kpresenter; <guimenuitem>Create Memory Stick Slideshow...</"
"guimenuitem> menu selection.</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:320
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will bring up the <guilabel>Create Memory Stick Slideshow</guilabel> "
"dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: guides.docbook:325
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>The &kpresenter; <guilabel>Create Memory Stick Slideshow</"
"guilabel> dialog.</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: guides.docbook:331
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase>The &kpresenter; <guilabel>Create Memory Stick Slideshow</guilabel> "
"dialog.</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:336
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Path</guilabel> is the folder in which your presentation will "
"be exported to as folders (<filename>DCIM</filename> and <filename>MSSONY</"
"filename>, see the <link linkend=\"ms-export-directory-structure\">folder "
"structure diagram</link> above) will be created. If you are able to, you may "
"wish to export directly to the <trademark>Memory Stick</trademark>, in which "
"case you would enter the location of the medium here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:347
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Title</guilabel> is used for both the name of the index file, "
"and as a text label on the title slide. Note that this title does not affect "
"the titles on any of the normal presentation slides - the title slide is "
"visible using the Sony projector setup prior to starting the actual "
"presentation display."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:355
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the <guibutton>Set Colors</guibutton> option to expand the dialog:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: guides.docbook:359
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>The &kpresenter; <guilabel>Create Memory Stick Slideshow</"
"guilabel> dialog (extended).</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: guides.docbook:365
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase>The &kpresenter; <guilabel>Create Memory Stick Slideshow</guilabel> "
"dialog (extended).</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:370
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These two color selectors are only used for the title slide. It can be "
"useful to change the title slides to make the presentations easier to "
"identify when working on the projector, though it is perfectly safe to leave "
"them as default."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:377
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can then press the <guibutton>OK</guibutton> button to proceed with the "
"actual export process."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:385
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Your presentation will now be exported into the correct format, with the "
"following dialog informing you of the progress of this process:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: guides.docbook:391
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>The &kpresenter; <guilabel>Create Memory Stick Slideshow</"
"guilabel> progress dialog.</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: guides.docbook:397
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase>The &kpresenter; <guilabel>Create Memory Stick Slideshow</guilabel> "
"progress dialog.</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:402
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When the export is complete, you can select the <guibutton>Done</guibutton> "
"button, and the dialog will close."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:409
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you did not export the slideshow directly onto a <trademark>Memory Stick</"
"trademark>, you will need to copy the correct files onto the "
"<trademark>Memory Stick</trademark> before you can utilise the projector. As "
"noted above, you need to copy over the correct folders and files starting at "
"<filename>DCIM</filename> and <filename>MSSONY</filename> into the \"root\", "
"or <filename>/</filename> of the <trademark>Memory Stick</trademark>. It is "
"critical that the folder structure is maintained, and you may find it easier "
"to copy the whole of <filename>DCIM</filename> and <filename>MSSONY</"
"filename> folders."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:423
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If necessary, you can safely rename the index file (which is "
"<filename>Slideshow.SPP</filename> by default), however you cannot rename "
"the slide images, nor can you change the name of these folders, as these are "
"encoded into the index file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: guides.docbook:436
#, no-c-format
msgid "Creating &kpresenter; Templates"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:438
#, no-c-format
msgid "It is very easy to add new templates to &kpresenter;'s library."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:440
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have made a presentation in a style that you would like to use again, "
"you can save it as a template."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:443
#, no-c-format
msgid "This tutorial will show how we can make a new template and save it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:448
#, no-c-format
msgid "Open &kpresenter; and create a new document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:452
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To add a little sparkle to the blank slide, we can change the slide "
"background - do this by either going to <guimenu>Format</guimenu> > "
"<guimenuitem>Slide Background...</guimenuitem>, or by selecting the same "
"item from the &RMB; menu:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: guides.docbook:458
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>The &kpresenter; <guilabel>Slide Background</guilabel> dialog.</"
"screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: guides.docbook:464
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase>The &kpresenter; <guilabel>Slide Background</guilabel> dialog.</"
"phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:469
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"We want the background to look attractive, so let's add a background "
"gradient by using the drop-down menu, and then selecting the gradient colors "
"by clicking the colored boxes. Of course, you may choose to use an image as "
"a background by clicking the <guilabel>Picture</guilabel> tab: feel free to "
"experiment, but keep it beautiful!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: guides.docbook:476
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Choosing a slide background</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: guides.docbook:481
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Choosing a slide background</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:487
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The page should now have the background you desire. Create a text box, and "
"type a heading for your slide:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: guides.docbook:491
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Adding a Heading to the new template</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: guides.docbook:496
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Adding a Heading to the new template</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:500
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you are happy with your template, go to <menuchoice><guimenu>File</"
"guimenu> <guimenuitem>Template Manager</guimenuitem></menuchoice>:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: guides.docbook:504
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Template Manager</"
"guimenuitem></screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: guides.docbook:510
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Template Manager</guimenuitem></"
"phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:515
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This dialog box allows you to select where you would like your template to "
"be saved:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: guides.docbook:519
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Saving the new template</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: guides.docbook:524
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Saving the new template</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:528
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I highly recommend that you save the template in the <guilabel>Screen "
"Presentations</guilabel> group. You may call it whatever you wish, in this "
"case, my template is named <userinput>Tutorial_Template</userinput>. Once "
"you are happy with the settings, press <guibutton>OK</guibutton> to add your "
"custom template to the template collection."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: guides.docbook:536
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can now close the document you have been working on (there is no need to "
"save it). The next time you are presented with the startup dialog, your very "
"own template will be available to select!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: guides.docbook:541
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<screeninfo>Your new template in the &kpresenter; startup dialog.</"
"screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: guides.docbook:547
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Your new template in the &kpresenter; startup dialog.</phrase>"
msgstr ""
